  "conclusions": [
    {
      "topic": "generic_platform_boundary",
      "result": "TextWorldIO adds only typed putchar/printf to existing generic core/binary stdio. Formats come from initialized application memory via printfBytes; signedchar promotion and unsignedchar byte conversion are explicit. No printS/printI/evaluate/runRow/main leaf is admitted."
    },
    {
      "topic": "fault_and_stream_model",
      "result": "Application memory and stream are separate. writeBytes accepts the full byte list on success and a possibly partial prefix on error; flush/delivery remain separate. Nonzero prior error is retained. Unchecked putchar/printf returns do not imply successful host I/O. Theorems keep every modeled fault policy rather than assuming application output success."
    },
    {
      "topic": "source_execution_model",
      "result": "WorldSourceWith pure escape requires an actual finite ArraySourceCall proof and equal stream, not an application output premise. TextCallExecute once/execute soundness routes external calls, actual pure source trees or installed-body evaluation with checked arguments/return casts/scopes. Recursive world calls decrease rank; no numerical application primitive is substituted."
    },
    {
      "topic": "expressions_and_fail_closed_subset",
